                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game puts you in the role of a young boy that sets out on a quest to defeat Zealock, the evil villain that is trying to conquer Rosantica. Flynn and his best friend and island guardian Dex must stop the evil before it spreads across the land. The story itself is fairly basic, and if I'm being completely honest, it's bland, not much meat on the bones. It does give the player a path to follow, but it's not the most compelling reason to play this game. \n\nThe biggest draw for me is the absolutely gorgeous hand drawn world of Rosantica I explored! From lush forests, to underground caverns, from snow covered mountains to poisonous swamps, every level was a treat to the eyes. There was a lot of love put into crafting the levels, and that's evident in how lovely everything looked. I also have to give nod to the soundtrack, because it worked so well with the game. I found myself humming along a few times, and variety was great. From bright and cheery to dark and somber, there was a song that fit the mood. \n\nGameplay was a mixed bag for me, mostly because combat wasn't very compelling. It basically boils down to smacking an enemy repeatedly until their stun bar fills or they attacked and you dodged and repeated that until they died. I was able to just stand right up against the enemy and wait, which made things boring. I found myself just running by enemies unless I was forced to fight them. That's not to say it's all bad. Boss fights are very fun, although I wouldn't call them challenging. Bosses have a decent variety of attacks and they do put up more of a fight than the regular enemies so when it's time to go against one of them, I had a good time.\n\nCombat isn't without some of it's own depth, too. There are three different weapons to choose from; a sword, axe, and claws. They attack at different speeds so mixing them up is fun initially. Once I unlocked the claws, that's all I really used because the speed was unmatched and it sped up combat. There's also a small, but decent skill tree that lets you unlock a longer attack strings, and some other buffs. Magic is another option! Ice, fire, and lightning are available to help during fights and I liked the addition. The one strange thing is the lack of Dex. It seems like she would be there to help during combat, but due to a story plot she's removed for a large portion of the game...and when you do get to use her, it's only on specific levels where you can summon her. I wished I could summon her when a bar filled, because it was cool getting to play alongside her...but in the way she's utilized now it felt empty.\n\nOverall, I'd recommend this game, but with some reservations. It's a solid adventure with combat that's fine, but doesn't really offer any real depth. The story is okay, but it's not compelling enough in my opinion. I think visually it's awesome and just running through the levels was great. Before you buy this game, just know it won't be much of a challenge for longtime fans of this genre, and in some ways it feels like it's lacking but damn if it doesn't try with all it's heart to offer some fun. [b]Final Rating: ⭐⭐⭐/5 (3/5). Solid, fun, but with flaws.[/B]",
